cent release that was healthy in production (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it was not used). Post-rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: root-cause the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15183, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01AYZJgcmNT2oiDvbiLTaLgo", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15183, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AYZJgcmNT2oiDvbiLTaLgo", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18514, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the latest release that was healthy in production. I skipped v2.3.1-rc because it was only ever healthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** All three regions now run v2.3.0, and a status check afterward shows the service healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is titled \"checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0.\" It records the failure, the rollback, the result after the rollback, and a follow-up to find the cause of the v2.3.1 problem before deploying it again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SdqAj3w1abYMpbUCWDsA9M", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id"